{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>His greatness, His mighty hand, and His outstretched arm.</b> Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra (on Deuteronomy 11:2) says: to bring you out of Egypt, and the signs and wonders that He did to Pharaoh, and what He did for you in the wilderness with the matter of the manna. But this is not correct in my eyes, for now He speaks only of the discipline with which HaShem disciplines those who transgress His will. <b>His greatness</b> — that He would exalt and magnify Himself, as in 'exalt Himself over me' (Exodus 8:5), 'tomorrow it shall be' (ibid. 8:19), and 'I will put a division' (ibid.), 'that you may know that the earth is HaShem's' (ibid. 9:29). <b>And His mighty hand</b> — 'and I will send My hand and smite Egypt' (ibid. 3:20), 'the great hand that HaShem did' (ibid. 14:31). <b>And His outstretched arm</b> — that He gave them no respite or deliverance from the time His hand was stretched out over them, and He did not withdraw His hand from devouring until He destroyed them. <b>And what He did to you in the wilderness</b> (Deuteronomy 11:5) — that He struck you with the calf and the fire of Taberah and the seraph serpents and the graves of craving and the plague at Shittim and the decree concerning the spies, in which the hand of HaShem was upon them until they came to this place. And He abbreviated concerning the punishments He brought upon them. If so, <b>and you shall keep all the commandment, in order that you may grow strong</b> — for His mighty hand strengthens those who keep His commandments, and He does not strengthen the hand of evildoers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:45.201880765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}